' QuickCart: incidents A/B/C
' Three failure scenarios defended with state transitions, retry logic,
' communication and business rules. Each @startuml block renders as its own image.

@startuml incident-A-payment-succeeded-ui-timed-out
title Incident A: Payment succeeded; UI timed out

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F2FAF5
skinparam noteBorderColor #8CC5A3

actor Customer
participant "QuickCart UI" as UI
participant "Checkout service" as Checkout
participant "Payment provider" as Pay

Customer -> UI : Place order
UI -> Checkout : POST /checkout\n(purchase_id = P-123)
Checkout -> Pay : Charge (idempotency key = P-123)
Pay --> Checkout : Charge succeeded
Checkout -> Checkout : Purchase P-123: PENDING -> PAID
UI -x Checkout : Response lost (UI timed out)
UI --> Customer : Request timed out

== Customer retries / refreshes ==
Customer -> UI : Retry
UI -> Checkout : GET /purchases/P-123/status\n(look up, do NOT resubmit checkout)

alt Outcome not yet known
  Checkout --> UI : PENDING
  UI --> Customer : "We are checking your payment"
  UI -> Checkout : Poll status of P-123 (same stable ID)
else Authoritative outcome known
  Checkout --> UI : PAID
  UI --> Customer : Order confirmed (P-123)
end

note over UI, Pay
  **Invariant:** do not create a second charge by blindly resubmitting checkout.
  The stable purchase ID is preserved across retries; any repeated charge
  call reuses the same idempotency key, so the provider returns the original result.
end note
@enduml

@startuml incident-B-hold-expired-payment-later-succeeded
title Incident B: Ten-minute hold expired; payment later succeeded

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F2FAF5
skinparam noteBorderColor #8CC5A3

actor Customer
participant "Checkout service" as Checkout
participant "Inventory\n(authority)" as Inv
participant "Payment provider" as Pay

Customer -> Checkout : Start checkout (P-456)
Checkout -> Inv : Place 10-minute hold on unit
Inv --> Checkout : Hold H-1 (expires in 10 min)

... 10 minutes pass ...
Inv -> Inv : Hold H-1: HELD -> EXPIRED\n(unit released)

Pay --> Checkout : Payment succeeded (late)
Checkout -> Pay : Verify payment for P-456
Pay --> Checkout : Confirmed PAID
Checkout -> Inv : Recheck availability (inventory is the authority)

alt Unit available
  Checkout -> Inv : Fresh atomic allocation for P-456\n(according to policy)
  Inv --> Checkout : Allocated
  Checkout -> Checkout : P-456: PAID -> ALLOCATED
  Checkout --> Customer : Order confirmed
else No unit available
  Checkout -> Checkout : P-456: PAID -> NEEDS_RECONCILIATION
  Checkout --> Customer : Offer alternative or refund (as agreed)
  opt Customer chooses refund
    Checkout -> Pay : Refund P-456
    Pay --> Checkout : Refunded
  end
end

note over Checkout, Pay
  **Invariant:** paid does not mean inventory is reserved.
  An expired hold is never treated as still valid.
end note
@enduml

@startuml incident-C-cancellation-after-shipment
title Incident C: Customer requests cancellation; item is shipped

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F2FAF5
skinparam noteBorderColor #8CC5A3

actor Customer
participant "Order service" as Order
participant "Shipment system\n(authority)" as Ship
participant "Returns process" as Returns

Customer -> Order : Request cancellation (P-789)
Order -> Ship : Get committed shipment state for P-789
Ship --> Order : Committed state

alt Not yet shipped
  Order -> Ship : Cancel shipment
  Ship --> Order : Cancelled
  Order --> Customer : Order cancelled
else SHIPPED (terminal transition)
  Order --> Customer : Already shipped; cancellation not possible.\nStarting a return instead
  Order -> Returns : Open return for P-789
  Returns --> Customer : Return instructions
end

note over Order, Returns
  **Invariant:** a terminal shipment transition must be respected.
  Never pretend a pre-shipment cancellation is possible once shipped.
end note
@enduml
